# Everything generated lives in build/ or tmp/ and nothing generated lives
# anywhere else. That is the rule; the patterns below are the safety net for
# when a tool ignores it.
build/
tmp/

# Wine prefix: 221MB, disposable, recreated by `make wine`.
spike/.wineprefix/
.wineprefix/

# Build output, wherever it escapes to. Open Watcom drops .err listings beside
# the SOURCE unless -fr= says otherwise, which is how win/ collected two.
*.exe
*.o
*.obj
*.lst
*.map
*.err

# Timestamped backups. Git is the backup -- every one of the 21 that
# accumulated here had its source in history, including two whose source file
# had been deleted entirely.
*.bak.*
*.bak[0-9].*
*.pre-*
# Taken before rebuilding a generated artefact -- vm/tools.iso and friends.
# The ISO is itself generated and ignored, so its snapshot has no business
# in history either.
*.bak-*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Editor
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# VM: disk images, install media, screenshots, and the scratch the driving
# scripts leave behind. The images are gigabytes and are NOT reproducible from
# this repo -- they are deliberately untracked, not deliberately disposable.
vm/*.qcow2
vm/*.qcow2.*
vm/*.raw
vm/*.raw.*
vm/*.img
vm/*.iso
vm/*.ppm
vm/*.png
vm/*.pid
vm/*.log
vm/sitter/
vm/watch/
vm/tools-stage/
vm/*.partial.*

# NOT ignored, deliberately: win/gaston.ini is the template config, and
# the guest's own runtime copy now lands beside its exe in build/win/, which
# is ignored by the first rule in this file.

# Running the client (or a check, under its own name) from the repo root drops
# its log here. The binaries are right to log -- that is what they are for --
# but the log is scratch, not source. /retroclaude.log is from before the
# rename, and still sits in older checkouts.
/gaston.log
/retroclaude.log
*.log
# And the SHOUTED form. gitignore is case-sensitive on Linux, so `*.log`
# never matched PROBE.LOG -- which is the 8.3 name the guest binaries write
# and the name it lands under when one is run from the repo root under
# Wine. It was swept into a commit by a `git add -A` before anybody noticed.
*.LOG
# The previous run, which rc_log_open renames the log to before it truncates
# it (win/core/log.cpp). Same reasoning as the line above and the same two
# spellings: the guest writes GREMOTE.PRV, a check run from the repo root
# writes netcheck.prv.
*.prv
*.PRV

# Claude Code transcript dumps. Large, and they are a record of a
# conversation rather than of this project.
/????-??-??-*-local-command-*.txt

# rpccheck.c's busy-JOB marker. Deleted at both ends of the run it takes part
# in; this is only for the crash that skips the second delete.
/rpccheck_marker.txt
.claude/

# Watcom ISO staging, like tools-stage: 90MB of unpacked third-party
# toolchain that the script rebuilds from the installer in seconds.
vm/*-stage/
